.........1.........2........
Sake keeps the syntax of
Ruby but writes the type on
every operation. This makes
the program a little longer,
yet every call says exactly
which code runs.
* Wrapping text is a classic
  exercise that is
  surprisingly full of
  corner cases.
* Extraordinarily-long-hyphe
  nated-identifiers-must-be-
  split-somewhere when they
  exceed the width.

  An indented paragraph
  keeps its indentation on
  every wrapped line, which
  matters for quoted text.
