.........1.........2.........3.........4.....
Sake keeps the syntax of Ruby but writes the
type on every operation. This makes the
program a little longer, yet every call says
exactly which code runs.
* Wrapping text is a classic exercise that is
  surprisingly full of corner cases.
* Extraordinarily-long-hyphenated-identifiers
  -must-be-split-somewhere when they exceed
  the width.

  An indented paragraph keeps its indentation
  on every wrapped line, which matters for
  quoted text.
